# Registry v2: the Legendary ceiling, per-era slots, transfer routes, eras, Skill Core open.
# Run on staging with NO other Legendary holder online or recorded (the counts below are server-wide); it advances the
# era twice, silently, and puts the era state back at the end (`era testmark` / `era testrestore`): test runs never
# reach Discord #story. Shipped knobs (design/data/skills.toml [legendary]): max_holders = 10 (the Ten Great Demon Lords),
# slots_per_era = 0 (no per-era throttle). `ttl registry legendcap <max> <slots>` replaces both until `legendcap reset`,
# so three bots can hit the ceiling (3) and the per-era slots (2).
# `registry legend` is the grant a rebirth Legend pick makes (opts.slot: spends a per-era slot); `ttl grant` is the admin
# grant (no slot, but the ceiling applies to it too). A second Legendary for an existing holder adds no holder.
# transfer(from, to, skill, route): at the ceiling it works when the receiver is already a holder or the giver stops
# being one; it never spends a slot; the route (duel, war, bequest, awakening, staff ...) lands in the history.
# A giver who is offline loses the record at once and the skill at their next login (berserker via TtlBotLegF).
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLegA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLegB
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLegC
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLegD
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLegE
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLegF
@sleep 2
ttl registry legendcap 3 2
ttl era testmark
ttl era next silent
ttl era expect slots 0
ttl era expect free 2
ttl registry legend TtlBotLegA great_sage
ttl registry legend TtlBotLegB predator
ttl era expect slots 2
ttl era expect free 0
ttl registry expect holders 2
ttl registry slots
# No slot left: the pick is refused; the admin grant is not (third holder, at the ceiling).
ttl registry legend TtlBotLegC creator
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegC creator false
ttl grant TtlBotLegC creator
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegC creator true
ttl registry expect holders 3
ttl era expect slots 2
# At the ceiling a fourth player gets nothing Legendary, not even from an admin; holders may collect more.
ttl grant TtlBotLegD envy
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegD envy false
ttl grant TtlBotLegB great_sage
ttl grant TtlBotLegC great_sage
ttl registry expect count great_sage 3
ttl registry expect holders 3
# Transfer at the ceiling: A (whose only Legendary it is) gives great_sage to D by duel; still 3 holders, no slot spent.
ttl registry transfer TtlBotLegA TtlBotLegD great_sage duel
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegA great_sage false
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegD great_sage true
ttl registry expect has TtlBotLegA great_sage false
ttl registry expect has TtlBotLegD great_sage true
ttl registry expect count great_sage 3
ttl registry expect holders 3
ttl registry expect last TtlBotLegD transfer great_sage
ttl registry expect moved TtlBotLegA TtlBotLegD great_sage
ttl registry expect routed TtlBotLegD great_sage duel
ttl era expect slots 2
ttl registry history great_sage
# Refused: B keeps predator, so great_sage to A would make a fourth holder; D already holds it; A no longer does.
ttl registry transfer TtlBotLegB TtlBotLegA great_sage war
ttl registry transfer TtlBotLegB TtlBotLegD great_sage war
ttl registry transfer TtlBotLegA TtlBotLegB great_sage war
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegB great_sage true
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegA great_sage false
ttl registry expect count great_sage 3
# Between holders any route works; the default route is staff.
ttl registry transfer TtlBotLegB TtlBotLegC predator bequest
ttl registry expect routed TtlBotLegC predator bequest
ttl registry transfer TtlBotLegC TtlBotLegB predator
ttl registry expect routed TtlBotLegB predator staff
# Offline giver (Rare, berserker): F holds it, goes offline; the record moves to A at once, by war.
ttl grant TtlBotLegF berserker
ttlbot remove TtlBotLegF
@sleep 1
ttl registry transfer TtlBotLegF TtlBotLegA berserker war
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegA berserker true
ttl registry expect has TtlBotLegA berserker true
ttl registry expect moved TtlBotLegF TtlBotLegA berserker
ttl registry expect routed TtlBotLegA berserker war
# Era titles, then the next era: slots free again, era titles cleared (ceiling raised for the rest).
ttl registry legendcap 10 2
ttl era title TtlBotLegE champion
ttl era expect titles TtlBotLegE 1
ttl era next silent
ttl era expect slots 0
ttl era expect free 2
ttl era expect titles TtlBotLegE 0
ttl registry legend TtlBotLegE wrath
ttl era expect slots 1
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotLegE wrath true
# Skill Cores never hold a Legendary and give E one more unique (wrath + the core's).
ttl core odds TtlBotLegE
ttl core open TtlBotLegE
ttl core expect TtlBotLegE 2
ttl era
# Clean up: back to the shipped knobs; resets free every record (F is respawned so its pending take-back is settled).
ttl registry legendcap reset
ttl era testrestore
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLegF
@sleep 3
ttl reset TtlBotLegA
ttl reset TtlBotLegB
ttl reset TtlBotLegC
ttl reset TtlBotLegD
ttl reset TtlBotLegE
ttl reset TtlBotLegF
ttlbot remove TtlBotLegA
ttlbot remove TtlBotLegB
ttlbot remove TtlBotLegC
ttlbot remove TtlBotLegD
ttlbot remove TtlBotLegE
ttlbot remove TtlBotLegF
